A||N||3||turbo86se||motor mount question||||5||
Z||000000||turbo86se||06-29-2000||06:56 PM||||I just got back from my mechanic's house, to see how my V6 conversion is going on my T-Top 88 coupe. He showed me the mounts on the cradle which I will be able to use, but there is an engine mount that I need to get. On the 4-cyl engine, it's long and is on the tranny side. Which motor mount is this?  He has one from an 86, but it won't work. It's an automatic tranny if it helps, and I'm installing a 56K mile '88 Formula V6.<BR>I hope you know what I'm trying to describe!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">   TIA ||||reg||5
Z||000001||ThatRickGuy||06-29-2000||07:28 PM||||Turbo, I just pulled my engine('88 formula auto) so it's still fresh in my mind. There are a bunch of bolts to the bell housing, like 6 or 7, and then there is 1 'U' shaped mount up front, it's pretty tall, bolts to the front of the block just left and lower then the water pump, and on the right side kinda by the AC bracket bolt holes. I'm pretty sure that any V6/auto mount should work as I beleive pontiac only used the 2.8 6cyl with the same tranny. I would suggest mounting it to the craddle first and then dropping the engin into it (you'll have to angle and wiggle a lot) because those 2 bolts are imposible to get to with the engine on it.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cooter||06-29-2000||07:46 PM||||On my 88's 3.4, I used all the original mounts- after swapping the 3.4's oil pan for the original 2.8 oil pan (and a new 2.8 oil pump)<BR>If you use the 3.4 pan on the 88, you have to "improvise" a new front motor mount. Ed Parks sells the mount already modified to work. <P>BTW- you can use the 3.4's cast manifolds (which have larger ports than the Fiero manifolds) if you know somebody that is good with a pipe bender.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Alex4mula||06-30-2000||02:35 PM||||Mmmm?? So that's the front motor mount that didn't work for me?? Ed provided me an L shaped mount that I could not use in my 88 Formula 3.4 swap. My engine did not have an oil pan so I used the 2.8 one. I used the 88 2.8 front mount but had to cut it for the A/C bracket. If some one needs it make an offer. Still I'm not sure if this is the mount that is related to the original post...||||reg||1
